Patch 2511: g_rsx_aa_mode edge smoothing, from the v0.15 backend (after 2510). For the full-screen scene copy (an
exact -1..1 box from 2510's box test) the backend asks the title port's hook for a mode for that target: 0 off,
1 FXAA, 2 stronger FXAA, 3 SMAA 1x (High preset, third_party_smaa, MIT, copied from the v0.15 toolkit). The replay
runs the pass right after that draw, once a frame: copy the target, then a full-screen pass back into it (SMAA: edge
detection, blending weights, neighbourhood blending into two scratch targets). The HUD drawn next stays sharp. Same
root signature as the game's draws: the passes use SRV windows at heap slot 96 (three of 16) and bind s0 to the
point/clamp sampler and s1 to a linear/clamp one; the next game draw rebinds its targets and samplers.

Tested (US disc): see the J-Stars STATUS entry for the feature build with this patch.

